⭐ Day 2 — Full Answers to All 20 Networking Interview Questions
🔵 1. Explain the difference between /16, /24, and /32 CIDR blocks.
/16 → 65,536 IPs → large network (VPC-level)

/24 → 256 IPs → typical subnet size

/32 → 1 IP → used for identifying a single host (e.g., route entries, firewall rules)

CIDR controls how many bits are used for the network portion.

🔵 2. Why do cloud providers use private IP ranges like 10.0.0.0/8?
Because private IPs:

Don’t require public IPv4 allocation

Are secure (not routable on the internet)

Allow massive internal networks

Enable VPC isolation

Clouds map private IPs → public IPs using NAT.

🔵 3. What is the purpose of a subnet, and how does it improve network design?
Subnets:

Segment networks for security

Control routing

Separate public/private workloads

Reduce broadcast domains

Allow fine-grained access control

Clouds use subnets to isolate workloads (DB, app, bastion).

